Ginger 1.0.1 classroom floor planner.
Quiet dedication: CEA practice associated with Dr. Donna Matteson. Not Autodesk. Not a Revit file.

Drawing model (vertices, lines, holes on a line, areas from closed walls, items, properties, schedules)
follows the element pattern of cvdlab/react-planner (MIT):
https://github.com/cvdlab/react-planner
Copyright (c) 2016-2020 CVDLAB
Original implementation. Ginger does not ship that app, its Redux store, or three.js.

Plan symbols (table, bed, chair, sofa, toilet, sink, door swing, window) are original marks
in the same categories as 1337GameDev/FloorPlanSVGSymbols (MIT, Copyright (c) 2023 Richard Duerr):
https://github.com/1337GameDev/FloorPlanSVGSymbols
Path data from that set is not copied.

Quaternius and Kenney meshes are not in this build. The 3D peek is a canvas picture so Chromebooks stay light.

No student names. Plans stay in the browser as .ginger.json.
